# Line endings are LF everywhere, including in the working tree on Windows.
#
# This is not a style preference. Every byte count in this repository's records —
# the §7 baselines in each contract, the 5,173 in the contact-page review, the
# figures in docs/review/ — is a check that only works if the files on disk are
# the files that were measured. Git's core.autocrlf on Windows rewrites LF to
# CRLF the next time it touches the tree, which silently moves every one of them
# and makes the byte-count discipline measure nothing.
#
# See docs/note/note_20260919_crlf_and_byte_count_discipline.md

* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files whose byte counts are asserted in records.
*.html  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.xml   text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
.htaccess text eol=lf
